  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer HfO2/SiO2 alternating dielectric stack on fused silica substrate. Initialize layer thicknesses with bimodal distribution: odd layers (HfO2) centered at 145 nm ± 15 nm, even layers (SiO2) centered at 75 nm ± 10 nm. Set total physical thickness maximum bound 15% higher than iteration 13 baseline. Optimize over 300-1700 nm wavelength range with coherent smatrix solver. Maximize mean transmittance in 1000-1700 nm band and mean reflectance in 300-450 nm band simultaneously. Apply gradient_thickness optimizer with relative uniform tolerance model. Layer sequence: HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2 (24 layers total, starting with HfO2 on substrate). Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: low transmission in 300-450 nm; low reflection in 1000-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count <= 30; materials restricted to HfO2 and SiO2.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 stack on fused silica using coherent smatrix. Maximize mean transmittance from 1000 to 1700 nm and mean reflectance from 300 to 450 nm. Initial thicknesses are 145 nm (HfO2) and 75 nm (SiO2) with 12% relative uniform tolerance. All 24 layers are optimizable within broad positive bounds.",
